&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role at impact.com&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a detail-oriented Growth Enablement Developer (Mid-Level) to join our Marketplace Growth team, supporting both advanced email development and technical messaging integrations across lifecycle and bulk communications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is suited to someone with solid foundational experience in HTML/CSS email development who is ready to take on greater ownership of complex builds, API-triggered messaging, and automation workflows within a fast-paced growth technology environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will be responsible for building and maintaining responsive, dynamic email templates, campaign assets, and triggered messaging flows, ensuring high-quality execution across both bulk and lifecycle communications. This includes working with more complex logic, modular components, and scalable template structures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to email development, you will actively support and contribute to API-triggered messaging and system integrations, working with platforms such as SendGrid and Marketo to help deliver event-based and automated customer journeys.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will collaborate closely with the Growth Enablement, Product, Data, and Development teams to translate requirements into well-structured, testable, and reliable messaging outputs. You will also play a more active role in debugging, optimisation, and improving end-to-end campaign and trigger performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for someone who is technically confident, detail-driven, and ready to work more independently across both email development and marketing automation systems, while continuing to grow into more senior technical ownership within the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and implement responsive HTML email templates, including complex and dynamic email structures based on design and lifecycle requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and support advanced dynamic emails, including conditional logic, personalization, and modular components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support implementation of API-triggered and event-based messaging, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configuring and maintaining triggered email templates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting API request setup and troubleshooting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Validating payload structure, data mapping, and output accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in integrating messaging platforms such as SendGrid with internal systems and workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform advanced QA and testing, including:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-client email rendering validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triggered send verification and API response checks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data accuracy and segmentation validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently monitor and troubleshoot issues in automated and triggered messaging flows, escalating only complex system-level issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and improve template libraries, modular components, and technical documentation standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure timely, accurate delivery of both bulk and automated lifecycle communications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively contribute to improvements in:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;API integration workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation logic and scalability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Email development standards and component design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-assisted tools to improve efficiency in:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Debugging and QA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Code optimisation and refactoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Template and component development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong HTML/CSS for email development and responsive design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;APIs (REST, JSON payloads, headers)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Webhooks and event-driven messaging systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with ESPs such as:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SendGrid&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Marketo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using tools such as Postman for API testing and validation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with QA/testing tools such as Litmus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data mapping and event tracking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Segmentation logic and dynamic content&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation workflows across lifecycle systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using AI tools (e.g. code assistants, debugging support, testing acceleration tools) as part of development workflow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to deepen expertise in integration architecture and messaging automation systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of experience in email development, CRM technology, marketing automation, or frontend/integration-focused roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience delivering end-to-end email builds and lifecycle campaign assets independently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to API integrations, triggered messaging, or automation systems in a production environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant diploma/degree or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mindset &amp;amp; Attributes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong ownership mindset with the ability to deliver work independently with minimal supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly detail-oriented, ensuring accuracy across both code and data-driven messaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curious and confident working across both technical and marketing domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive problem-solver who can diagnose and resolve issues across build, data, and delivery layers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using AI tools responsibly to improve speed and quality without compromising standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and effective across CRM, product, data, and development teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously improving technical depth in APIs, automation, and messaging systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
