&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Role at &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://impact.com&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;impact.com&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;strong&gt;:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As we scale toward 600 product engineers, the infrastructure layer that powers everything - Kubernetes clusters, VPCs, compute pools, storage, shared services - becomes mission-critical. Right now, that infrastructure is the single point of failure for every developer-facing capability the platform team builds. You&#39;ll be the senior IC responsible for designing, deploying and operating that substrate. This is more than infrastructure management; it&#39;s production-quality software engineering applied to infrastructure. You&#39;ll build abstractions that let service teams specify their infrastructure requirements at a high level, then turn those into reliable, secure, performant deployments. This role sits at the intersection of deep cloud-native expertise and solid software engineering discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design, deployment and operation of platform-layer infrastructure: VPCs, compute pools, storage, Kubernetes clusters, and the networking that connects them - translating configuration data into inputs for IaC modules provided by Cloud Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the monitoring and operation of managed pub/sub messaging systems (e.g. Kafka) that service teams depend on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve abstractions that allow service teams to express infrastructure requirements at a high level, translating those into production-grade deployments with security and high availability baked in by default.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate platform infrastructure at 99.9% uptime. Own the change management process for infrastructure changes and drive a &amp;gt; 95% change success rate. Build a strong post-incident learning loop.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Cloud Operations to consume their IaC modules and feed back operational lessons and enhancement requests. Maintain a clean module-consumer relationship that protects both functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anchor the technical standards for the Shared Services and Infrastructure team: code review quality bar, controller patterns, GitOps idioms, IaC consumption patterns and operational runbooks. &lt;br&gt;Mentor junior engineers and set the bar for infrastructure software engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You &lt;em&gt;Bring: &lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Software or infrastructure engineering experience, including operating production Kubernetes and cloud-native infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software-engineering fundamentals and hands-on experience with Java.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep Kubernetes expertise and comfort with Linux command line.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong networking and cloud architecture fluency: VPCs, subnets, load balancing, security, service mesh interaction.&lt;/li&gt;
